findings.description:
Elisabeth Myslisch probably married Anton Netzel on 2 February 1845 at Oxhöft, Putzig, West Prussia. The church entry indexes the groom as born about 1808 and the bride as Elisabeth Desmer, born about 1805. The identification is probable, not proved, and rests on correlation:

- the same parish;
- a first child born 19 Oct 1845 and baptised at Oxhöft about nine months after the wedding;
- the couple's children's baptisms (1845, 1847, 1850) naming the mother Elisabeth Myslisch / Myslisz / Eva Myslisck;
- no other marriage of an Anton Netzel to a Myslisch being indexed.

Whether the bride was a widow née Myslisch is not established. The register image is access-restricted.
